post_install() {
  cat <<'EOS'
PhigrAuth is a TTY greeter. When started by greetd it automatically uses the
greetd IPC socket (GREETD_SOCK) for PAM authentication and session start, so
it can run as an unprivileged greeter user under cage. Standalone/root PAM
mode is also available (auth_backend = "pam").
See /usr/share/doc/phigrauth/README.md and config.example.toml.

For UI development only:
  PHIGRAUTH_DEV_PASSWORD=test phigrauth --windowed --dry-power --dev-mock
EOS
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  :
}
